GolangTAKServer is the native TAK service for the Pi 5 image.

It runs without Docker under OpenWrt procd and stores its configuration,
certificates, users, logs, and data under /opt/golangtakserver. During the
initial OpenMANET setup wizard, the password entered for the system root
account is also used for the GoLangTAKServer administrator account named
root. The password is passed through a temporary UCI value and removed after
the account update succeeds; the one-way password hash in /etc/shadow is not
read or copied. Complete the wizard with a non-empty password before using
the TAK dashboard.

The secure TAK listener is TLS 8089. The dashboard and enrollment endpoints use
HTTPS 8443 and 8446. Plain TCP, UDP, and HTTP are disabled in the default
profile. Port 8080 is intentionally unused by this service. Create client
connection packages or QR codes from the dashboard.

The packaged binary is GolangTAKServer 1.6.3 for Linux ARM64, built from the
upstream `golangtakserver-v1.6.3` source with the OpenMANET QR layout fix. Its
upstream license is installed at /opt/golangtakserver/LICENSE.
